OL,3,ATwo men killed by falling trees as
OL,4,AStorm Boelo leaves 160,000 properties
OL,5,Awithout power
OL,6,
OL,7,FTwo men have been killed by falling
OL,8,Ftrees on Sunday as Storm Boelo
OL,9,Fcontinues to bring severe weather to
OL,10,Fthe UK.
OL,12,FA man in his 20s was pronounced dead in
OL,13,Fnorth London after the car he was
OL,14,Fdriving was hit by a falling tree. It
OL,15,Fcame hours after a 60-year-old man died
OL,16,Fin Dumfries and Galloway, Scotland.
OL,18,FThe harsh weather battering the UK had
OL,19,Fleft 161,400 properties without power
OL,20,Fas of 15:00 GMT on Sunday afternoon,
OL,21,Fthe Energy Networks Association (ENA)
OL,22,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
